#: ../../../developer.rst:119
msgid "Rules to Write By"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:121
msgid ""
"It is important to refer to things and concepts by their most specific name. "
"When writing xonsh code or documentation please use technical terms "
"appropriately. The following rules help provide needed clarity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:126
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:128
msgid "User-facing APIs should be as generic and robust as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:129
msgid "Tests belong in the top-level ``tests`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:130
msgid "Documentation belongs in the top-level ``docs`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:133
msgid "Expectations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:135
msgid "Code must have associated tests and adequate documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:136
msgid ""
"User-interaction code (such as the Shell class) is hard to test. Mechanism "
"to test such constructs should be developed over time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:138
msgid "Have *extreme* empathy for your users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:139
msgid ""
"Be selfish. Since you will be writing tests you will be your first user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:142
msgid "Python Style Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:144
msgid ""
"xonsh follows `PEP8 <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/>`_ for all "
"Python code. The following rules apply where `PEP8 <https://www.python.org/"
"dev/peps/pep-0008/>`_ is open to interpretation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:147
msgid ""
"Use absolute imports (``import xonsh.tools``) rather than explicit relative "
"imports (``import .tools``). Implicit relative imports (``import tools``) "
"are never allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:150
msgid ""
"We use sphinx with the numpydoc extension to autogenerate API documentation. "
"Follow the `numpydoc <https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format."
"html#docstring-standard>`_ standard for docstrings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:152
msgid "Simple functions should have simple docstrings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:153
msgid ""
"Lines should be at most 80 characters long. The 72 and 79 character "
"recommendations from PEP8 are not required here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:155
msgid ""
"Tests should be written with `pytest <https://docs.pytest.org/>`_ using a "
"procedural style. Do not use unittest directly or write tests in an object-"
"oriented style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:157
msgid "Test generators make more dots and the dots must flow!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:158
msgid ""
"We use `ruff <https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/>`_ for linting and formatting the "
"code. It is used as a `pre-commit <https://pre-commit.com/>`_ hook. Enable "
"it by running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:160
msgid ""
"pre-commit install\n"
"pre-commit run --all-files"
msgstr ""

