#: ../../../developer.rst:179
msgid "Running the Tests - Basic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:181
msgid ""
"Run all the tests using pytest. Use ``python -m pytest`` to prevent using "
"xonsh code from ``site-packages`` if xonsh was installed in the same "
"environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:183
msgid "python -m pytest -q"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:187
msgid ""
"Use \"-q\" to keep pytest from outputting a bunch of info for every test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:190
msgid "Running the Tests - Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:192
msgid "To perform all unit tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:194
msgid "python -m pytest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:198
msgid ""
"If you want to run specific tests you can specify the test names to execute. "
"For example to run test_aliases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:201
msgid "python -m pytest test_aliases.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:205
msgid "Note that you can pass multiple test names in the above examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:207
msgid "python -m pytest test_aliases.py test_environ.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:212
msgid "Running the Tests in Parallel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:214
msgid ""
"On a multi-core machine `pytest-xdist <https://pypi.org/project/pytest-xdist/"
">`_ runs tests several times faster by distributing work across worker "
"processes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:218
msgid ""
"pip install pytest-xdist\n"
"python -m pytest -n auto"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:223
msgid ""
"``-n auto`` uses one worker per CPU core. Pass an explicit integer (``-n "
"4``) to cap the worker count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:227
msgid "Writing the Tests - Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:229
msgid "(refer to pytest documentation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:231
msgid ""
"With the Pytest framework you can use bare ``assert`` statements on anything "
"you're trying to test, note that the name of the test function has to be "
"prefixed with ``test_``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:235
msgid ""
"def test_whatever():\n"
"    assert is_true_or_false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:240
msgid ""
"The conftest.py in tests directory defines fixtures for mocking various "
"parts of xonsh for more test isolation. For a list of the various fixtures:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:243
msgid "python -m pytest --fixtures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:247
msgid ""
"when writing tests it's best to use pytest features i.e. parametrization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:249
msgid ""
"@pytest.mark.parametrize('env', [test_env1, test_env2])\n"
"def test_one(env, xession):\n"
"    # update the environment variables instead of setting the attribute\n"
"    # which could result in leaks to other tests.\n"
"    # each run will have the same set of default env variables set.\n"
"    xession.env.update(env)\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:259
msgid ""
"this will run the test two times each time with the respective ``test_env``. "
"This can be done with a for loop too but the test will run only once for the "
"different test cases and you get less isolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:263
msgid ""
"With that in mind, each test should have the least ``assert`` statements, "
"preferably one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:266
msgid "At the moment, xonsh doesn't support any pytest plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:268
msgid "Happy Testing!"
msgstr ""

