#: ../../../developer.rst:424
msgid "Testing xonsh on Different Operating Systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:427
msgid "Nix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:429
msgid ""
"If you have Nix package manager installed on your system, you can use it "
"instead of Docker to build and run your \"work in progress version\". If Nix "
"is configured with experimental features ``nix-command`` and ``flakes`` "
"enabled, it is as simple as running this in the project directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:434
msgid ""
"# build and run with a single command\n"
"nix run\n"
"\n"
"# or build and then run\n"
"nix build  # this builds the package and creates a `result` symlink\n"
"./result/bin/xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:443
msgid ""
"This will build and run the current state of the repository with Nix. "
"Optionally add ``-L`` to the Nix commands to see detailed output when "
"building. If you have new files created and need them to build, make sure "
"they're added to Git (e.g. using ``git add``), or Nix won't be aware of them "
"when building the package from flake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:448
msgid "If you prefer not to use flakes, it can also be done in a legacy way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:450
msgid ""
"nix-build nix/ -A xonsh\n"
"./result/bin/xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:455
msgid ""
"The default Python version used follows the default of ``nixpkgs-unstable`` "
"(it is 3.13 at the time of writing this). There are variants using different "
"Python versions declared in ``nix/default.nix``. For example, to use Python "
"3.14:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:459
msgid ""
"# build and run\n"
"nix run '.#xonsh-py314'\n"
"\n"
"# build only\n"
"nix build '.#xonsh-py314'\n"
"\n"
"# build with legacy nix\n"
"nix-build nix/ -A xonsh-py314"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:472
msgid "Binary cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:474
msgid ""
"Building xonsh from the flake compiles it from source, which takes a while. "
"Every push to ``main`` is built by CI and the results are pushed to the "
"`xonsh.cachix.org <https://app.cachix.org/cache/xonsh>`_ binary cache. To "
"use it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:478
msgid "nix run nixpkgs#cachix -- use xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:482
msgid "Or declare the substituter yourself, e.g. on NixOS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:484
msgid ""
"nix.settings = {\n"
"  substituters = [ \"https://xonsh.cachix.org\" ];\n"
"  trusted-public-keys = [ \"xonsh.cachix.org-1:"
"wwdHGMixIz1oZB0MtubjhZyCfWMWRLTQTT9zLO+DyMY=\" ];\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:491
msgid ""
"The ``cachix`` branch always points at the newest commit of ``main`` that "
"was built successfully, so following it guarantees a cache hit instead of a "
"local build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:495
msgid "nix run github:xonsh/xonsh/cachix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:501
msgid "Container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:503
msgid ""
"It is often useful to try xonsh in a clean environment on a distribution "
"other than your own — for example to reproduce a bug report or to validate a "
"change against a pristine setup. The recipes below use rootless ``podman`` "
"containers; ``docker`` would work just as well if you prefer it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:510
msgid "Script to run in Container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:512
msgid ""
"If you want to run your \"work in progress version\" without installing and "
"in a fresh environment you can use Docker. If Docker is installed you just "
"have to run this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:516
msgid "python xonsh-in-docker.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:520
msgid ""
"This will build and run the current state of the repository in an isolated "
"container (it may take a while the first time you run it). You can override "
"the default Python and ``prompt_toolkit`` versions with ``--python`` and ``--"
"ptk``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:525
msgid "python xonsh-in-docker.py --python 3.13 --ptk 3.0.52"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:529
msgid ""
"Ensure your cwd is the root directory of the project (i.e., the one "
"containing the .git directory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:533
msgid "Nix Container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:535
msgid ""
"podman run --rm -it nixos/nix\n"
"nix-channel --update && nix-shell -p xonsh\n"
"xonsh\n"
"xcontext"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer.rst:543
msgid "Arch Linux Container"
msgstr ""

